    question: 'What is the best productivity app for remote workers?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Notion</strong> is our top overall pick for remote workers. It combines notes, tasks, databases, and wikis in one flexible workspace. For pure task management, <strong>Todoist</strong> is unbeatable—simple, fast, and available everywhere. <strong>Obsidian</strong> is best for knowledge workers who take extensive notes.</p><p>The "best" app depends on your workflow. If you need team collaboration, Notion excels. For personal task management, Todoist or Things 3 shine. For building a personal knowledge base, Obsidian is unmatched.</p>'
